{"exit_status": "escalated", "ai_message": "AP escalation and audit documentation needed: record PAY-INV-777666-8000 as an unauthorized $8,000 ACH that platform confirms cleared November 24, 2026 and cannot be reversed; investigate the earlier May 1, 2024 tool timestamp; assess recovery/corrective action. Maintain the hold on the remaining $2,000 until the 20 backordered units are received and reconciled. No additional payment is authorized.", "human_response": "Record PAY-INV-777666-8000 as an unauthorized $8,000 ACH, confirmed cleared on November 24, 2026, and unrecoverable through reversal. The May 1, 2024 tool timestamp predates this payment by more than two years; treat it as a likely timestamp or audit-log integrity issue, preserve the original record, and escalate it for investigation rather than using it as the payment date.

Please open an AP/fraud incident, retain the payment confirmation and related PO, receipt, invoice, and approval records, and notify Treasury, AP leadership, and the appropriate compliance team. Ask the bank and supplier about recovery or credit options, and document the outcome; do not represent the payment as recoverable unless confirmed. Review access, approval, and payment-control logs to identify how the unauthorized ACH was initiated and prevent recurrence.

Keep the remaining $2,000 on hold until all 20 backordered units are received and reconciled against the PO and invoice. No further payment is authorized."}
